    "q-221908": {
      "dom_id": "step-q221908",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nThe notation $4∣16$ means {{field-1}}. It is equivalent to the statement that there exists {{field-2}} $k$ such that {{field-3}}.",
      "worked_solution": "The notation $a∣b$ means $a$ divides $b.$ So, $4∣16$ means $4\\text{ divides }16.$\n\nAccording to the definition of integer divisibility, the fact that $a$ divides $b$ means that there exists an integer $k$ such that \n\n$$\nb=ak.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $4∣16$ is equivalent to the statement that there exists $\\text{an integer}$ $k$ such that $16=4k.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
