    "q-221915": {
      "dom_id": "step-q221915",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nThe notation $7∤8$ means {{field-1}}. It is equivalent to the statement that {{field-2}}{{field-3}} $k,$ we have {{field-4}}.",
      "worked_solution": "The notation $a∤b$ means $a$ does not divides $b.$ So, $7∤8$ means $7\\text{ doesn't divide }8.$\n\nAccording to the definition of integer divisibility, the fact that $a$ does not divide $b$ means that for any integer $k,$ we have that \n\n$$\nb\\ne ak.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $7∤8$ is equivalent to the statement that $\\text{for any}$ $\\text{integer}$ $k,$ we have $8\\ne 7k.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "select",
          "dom_id": "selectList-221915-0",
          "tag": "custom-select",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "0",
              "dom_id": null,
